[32m+[m[32m# Resume site starter[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAstro resume site for Workshop 1. Edit one file, preview locally, publish with GitHub Pages.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**In class:** open [`WORKSHOP.md`](./WORKSHOP.md) in VS Code and check steps off by changing `- [ ]` to `- [x]` in the editor (or use the online student walkthrough your facilitator shares).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Personalize[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEdit `src/data/profile.js`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Name, role, about, skills, links[m
[32m+[m[32m- Education, coursework, activities, experience, projects[m
[32m+[m[32m- Leave any list as `[]` if you do not have that content yet — empty sections stay hidden[m
[32m+[m[32m- Replace every `example.com` placeholder with your real URLs[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOptional photo: add `public/photo.jpg`, then set `photo: '/photo.jpg'`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Preview locally[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm install[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen the local URL printed in the terminal (usually `http://localhost:4321`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Print / ATS PDF[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse **Print / ATS PDF** to open the browser print dialog. The sidebar hides and you get a clean single-column PDF.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Connect to GitHub (workshop path)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Create an **empty Public** repository on GitHub (**no** README, **no** .gitignore, **no** license).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Push this folder with the commands in [`WORKSHOP.md`](./WORKSHOP.md) (or the online guide).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Expect a red X in **Actions** until you enable Pages — that is normal.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. After your pull request merges: **Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions**, then **Re-run** the failed workflow if needed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Example project entry[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach project can link to its own page at `/projects/your-slug/` with a walkthrough and screenshots. Put images in `public/projects/`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```js[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  title: 'Inventory helper',[m
[32m+[m[32m  slug: 'inventory-helper', // URL path; keep lowercase with hyphens[m
[32m+[m[32m  summary: 'Built a tracker that reduced stock-check time for a student org.',[m
[32m+[m[32m  overview: 'Short story of what the project is and who it helped.',[m
[32m+[m[32m  problem: 'What was painful before this existed.',[m
[32m+[m[32m  approach: [[m
[32m+[m[32m    'Talked to two officers about how they counted stock.',[m
[32m+[m[32m    'Built a spreadsheet-backed tracker in Python.',[m
[32m+[m[32m  ],[m
[32m+[m[32m  outcome: 'Stock checks dropped from ~45 minutes to under 15.',[m
[32m+[m[32m  skills: ['Python', 'Spreadsheets'],[m
[32m+[m[32m  link: 'https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY',[m
[32m+[m[32m  screenshots: [[m
[32m+[m[32m    {[m
[32m+[m[32m      src: '/projects/inventory-helper-1.svg',[m
[32m+[m[32m      alt: 'Tracker home screen',[m
[32m+[m[32m      caption: 'Main view officers used during events.',[m
[32m+[m[32m    },[m
[32m+[m[32m  ],[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSet `screenshots: []` if you do not have images yet.[m
